  "notes": "GAC (Guangzhou Automobile Group) trades in Australia as 'GAC' with the 'AION' (also styled Aion) sub-brand used for its BEV models. GAC Australia launched in November 2025 with three models (Aion V BEV, Emzoom petrol SUV, M8 PHEV people-mover), then added the Aion UT BEV hatch in March/April 2026, confirmed via GAC's official en-au site (gacgroup.com.au/en-au), CarExpert, Drive, EV Central, carsales, and NRMA. GAC also displayed the Aion V and Aion UT alongside GAC-badged (non-Aion) PHEV/ICE models (M8 PHEV, Emzoom) at the 2026 Melbourne Motor Show; those non-BEV GAC models are out of scope for this file. As of Sept 2026 only two Aion nameplates are sold new/orderable in Australia: Aion V (mid-size SUV, on sale since Nov 2025) and Aion UT (compact hatch, on sale since March 2026). No Aion Y, Hyptec, or other Aion-badged BEV was found confirmed for the Australian market. Official GAC Australia site (gacgroup.com.au/en-au) currently (Sept 2026, within the Q3 2026 order window) advertises the Aion UT Premium at a national drive-away price of $31,990 for orders placed 1 Jul-30 Sep 2026; CarExpert/Drive/EV Central report the standing (non-promotional) RRP as $31,990 (Premium) / $35,990 (Luxury) before on-road costs, which is what is recorded here as priceAud/priceBasis, with the current drive-away promo noted separately. Aion V DC charge rate variously reported at up to 180kW; Aion UT DC charge rate variously reported (thebeep: 87kW; CarExpert reviews emphasise a 24-minute 30-80% fast charge without stating a peak kW figure) - recorded dcChargeKw for Aion UT is lower-confidence.",
